// nullary **sum-variant literal** bodies are what the v3 lowerer rejects per
// ROADMAP.md:418 (→ `ValueBody::Unparsed` until structural validation exists).
// **Record-structural** bodies (→ `ValueBody::Structural`) **do** lower clean —
// they are **not** part of this gap. TS per-primitive D2a(3) instances would be
// top-level nullary-sum-variant literals (`data ts_*: TsEcma262PrimitiveOperationSemantics
// = TsNumberIeee754Binary64Semantics`), hence this deferral. Operation
// disposition rows expressed as **record-structural** bodies (variant tags
// only at **field** positions inside `Rec { … }`) are likewise class-5-SAFE.
// Fact-bundle grounding rows are **class-5-SAFE** when expressed as
// records; their absence is gated by the T-4 Phase-3 fact-bundle rework,
// not by `GroundingMap` home selection. **Deferred** operation instance
// rows remain gated by Class-5-Gap-3 / top-level-`ValueBody` substrate work
// (R2/R3 lane, ROADMAP.md:416/#418; #920 / #1017 / #1068). **Trigger** =
// that gap closes. The operation-semantics **TYPES** / classifiers +
// Practice-4 ledgers above are canonical regardless; instance rows
// land when the substrate can structurally validate **top-level** sum-variant
// `data` bodies.)


